  "report_period": "Week 39 (20th Sep to 27th Sep 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Chinese Maritime Transport have committed their Capesize \"China Peace\" 174/2005 SWS, China (SS/DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at region USD 20 mill. Note that a month ago, the one- year-younger sister vessel \"Maran Prosperity\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 21,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Martha\" 81/2014 Tadotsu, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 08/2027, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) of Nissen Kaiun was committed to clients of Sea Pioneer at USD 26,2 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger \"Nord Penguin\" 81/2015 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1C) was sold a month ago at USD 30,5 mill. Moreover, Nisshin Shipping committed their \"Vincent Triton\" 81/2020 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) to Greek interests at low USD 30 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Vincent Talisman\" 81/2020 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in May at low USD 33 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Zorina\" 57/2011 Zhejiang, China (SS/DD 12/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed at USD 13,8 mill, while the \"Diva\" 56/2011 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 14,75 mill. In addition, the \"Visayas\" 56/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 16,8 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Bright Hero\" 55/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in June at the same price. The Handysize \"Yochow\" 34/2015 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Greek interests at USD 19 mill. Note that earlier this month, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"African Egret\" 34/2016 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 21,75 mill.",
    "tankers": "Turkish owners committed their VLCC \"Advantage Virtue\" 296/2009 Bohai, China (SS 02/2029, DD 09/2026, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 51 mill. For reference, the Korean built \"C. Prosperity\" 313/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold back in June at USD 53,5 mill. The MR2 \"Elijah\" 45/2007 Bohai, China (SS 01/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Nigerian interests at region USD 21 mill. Remind you that back in February, the one-year-older \"Chang Hang Fa Xian\" 45/2006 Bohai (SS 09/2026, DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 19,9 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 13,000/16,000 pd. A number of and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 11,000/14,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 100K/200K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 17,750 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A generally quiet week for this segment. Trips from China into Continent via South Africa were reported at the level of usd 16,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 19,000/22,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 18,000/21,000 pd. An Ultramax was reported fixed in the usd 17,000 pd for 5/7 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into Indonesia were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. A number of and Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Continental trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Mediterranean trips Continent were fixed around usd 10,000/11,000 pd. US Gulf trips were reported at the level of usd 15,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
